        "original_id": "d26fd8d0-faf8-56df-96eb-560cc7ed10a7",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Jefferson Davis, Alexander H. Stephens, Franklin Pierce\n- Roles: President of the Confederate States, Vice President of the Confederate States, United States Secretary of War\n- Organizations: Confederate States of America, United States government\n- Systems: Provisional Confederate States Constitution\n\nFacts:\n- From 1853 to 1857, Jefferson Davis served as the 23rd United States Secretary of War under U.S. President Franklin Pierce.\n- Under the Provisional Confederate States Constitution, Jefferson Davis had been elected President and Alexander H. Stephens had been elected Vice President before their later election to permanent offices.\n- Jefferson Davis and Alexander H. Stephens were elected as the first permanent President and Vice President of the Confederate States of America for six-year terms running from February 22, 1862, to February 22, 1868.",
